{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786914767961},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Find the total number of farmers markets in the U.S. from the first dataset\n2. Use the census file to get the total U.S. population\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents to four decimal places\n4. Use tools for any math necessary\n5. Not mention unverified facts\n6. One confident sentence\n\nAccording to the AGENTS.md instructions, I need to:\n1. First check if semantic models exist using `xorq_semantic_models`\n2. Use `xorq_catalog_list_aliases` to see what's available\n3. If no existing alias covers the data, ingest the sources into the catalog\n4. Compose the necessary metric\n5. Use `xorq_select` to get the value\n6. Declare obligations and verify with `xorq_verify`\n7. Check lineage with `xorq_check_lineage`\n\nLet me start by checking what's in the catalog already.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents in the U.S. Let me start by checking the xorq catalog for existing data, then ingest and compute the metric."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01DhXbKEuK7dFXudNTKWL22Q","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01EEyU9ZESs4NyPmWjrCpGDr","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":389,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8161,"totalTokens":8560,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0019450000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01020125,"total":0.01215625},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":229},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914767982,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77jUfghqVGA7BSMotYz","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01DhXbKEuK7dFXudNTKWL22Q","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914773120},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01EEyU9ZESs4NyPmWjrCpGDr","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No aliases.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914773121},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both datasets. According to the xorq-catalog skill, I should:\n1. Create build scripts under `.xorq/scripts/`\n2. Use `xo.deferred_read_csv()` to read the data\n3. Build and add to the catalog\n\nLet me create two ingestion scripts - one for the farmers markets and one for the census data. Then I'll compose a metric alias that calculates the per-capita figure.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"No existing data. I'll ingest both sources and compute the metric. Let me create build scripts:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01NcNZsnTVzpDBopqFCk3bSK","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py","content":"import xo\n\ncon = None\nstorage_options = xo.FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"xorq-agent\"})\n\nexpr = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=storage_options\n)\n"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_018pjxezh8BrHF2zMp1kw9KM","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/census_2025.py","content"