2. Get the total U.S. population from census-2025 (filtering for the U.S. total)\n3. Calculate the per-capita metric: (total_markets / total_population) * 100000\n\nLet me first check what's in the census file to understand how to get the U.S. total. I should look at a few rows to see which one represents the U.S.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_014mFfQ2N5f2rh7RknK2ce9S","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"census-2025","compose":"source.select('NAME', 'POPESTIMATE2025').limit(10)"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":292,"cacheRead":17620,"cacheWrite":1468,"totalTokens":19394,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0014600000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0017620000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.001835,"total":0.005071},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":173},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914806219,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77nGtrJLpCvzEv54cNG","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_014mFfQ2N5f2rh7RknK2ce9S","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"NAME\",\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n\"United States\",341784857\n\"Northeast Region\",58042054\n\"New England\",15431980\n\"Middle Atlantic\",42610074\n\"Midwest Region\",69762666\n\"East North Central\",47693655\n\"West North Central\",22069011\n\"South Region\",133833983\n\"South Atlantic\",70198706\n\"East South Central\",20069188\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914811355},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see that \"United States\" is the first row with population 341,784,857. Now let me get the total number of farmers markets by summing the farmers_markets column.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01FdBBic1ZMzjLYRswSj5MSW","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers-markets","compose":"source.aggregate(total=source.farmers_markets.sum())"}}],"api":"anthropic-me